{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789496914,"nonce":"bSzhxfBZ033l/sJLhOn9vqRGZSQ=","message":"The same fixed-arity record limitation also affects module-level functions passed as values. It is now the next nbody_modified blocker after the range-alias signal fix in 100e2a9.\n\nMinimal reproducer:\n\n    def main(n, ref=\"sun\"):\n        print(n, ref)\n    def invoke(f):\n        f(1)\n    invoke(main)\n\nCPython prints `1 sun`; zypy raises `TypeError: function takes 2 positional arguments but 1 were given`.\n\nIn the unedited kernel, util.run_benchmark receives main as bench_func and calls bench_func(num_runs). Direct calls of offset_momentum and advance work, and after 20000 steps all five body states match CPython exactly. The harness callback is what blocks the run now.\n\nThe range-alias implementation adds a variadic record convention (arity -1, code receives the record plus a boxed argument list). This offers an argument-dispatch mechanism, but Python defaults still need correct definition-time evaluation and storage in the function record; simply evaluating them at callback invocation would be wrong.","files":null}]}